# Zerolog Log Formatting

Always split zerolog log calls across multiple lines when they chain `.Str()`, `.Err()`, `.Int()`, or similar fields with `.Msg()`.

Put the level (e.g. `log.Error()`, `log.Info()`) on the first line, each field on its own line, and `.Msg("...")` on the last line.

**Wrong** (single line):

```go
log.Error().Str("userID", user.ID.String()).Err(err).Msg("Failed to revoke session")
log.Info().Str("userID", user.ID.String()).Msg("Session revoked successfully")
```

**Correct** (multi-line):

```go
log.Error().
	Str("userID", user.ID.String()).
	Err(err).
	Msg("Failed to revoke session")

log.Info().
	Str("userID", user.ID.String()).
	Msg("Session revoked successfully")
```

Apply this pattern to `log.Error()`, `log.Info()`, `log.Warn()`, `log.Debug()`, and any other zerolog level when there is more than one chained call before `.Msg()`.
